msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Default video dragging behaviour:"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Moving through the timeline can be done with the scroll wheel, and scrolling between tracks can be done by holding SHIFT. Zooming in on the timeline can be done by holding CTRL and making the tracks bigger/smaller can be done with CTRL+SHIFT. "
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Editing in GoZen"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "The editing process is quite straight forward due to the minimalistic UI and functionality. There are some shortcuts to be aware of to make your editing more comfortable and the default position of those  shortcuts make it possible to keep your left hand on your keyboard and right hand on your mouse. Ergonomics are important."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Timeline mode shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "GoZen has 2 timeline modes. The default mode is for selecting/moving/... clips, the other mode cut clips where you clip. These modes can be toggled with shortcuts and is a fast way to edit your videos."
msgstr ""

