#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Focus on timeline:"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Effects and transitions inside of GoZen are very similar and their settings can both be accessed from the effects panel. Same is true for the settings of the text and color clips. Selecting a clip on the timeline will make that clip's effects visible in the effects panel and from there you can click the button to add effects, or use the shortcut CTRL+A to show the popup for adding effects."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Transitions can be created by hovering over the corners of clips, this will make the fading handles appear. Because clips can both contain visuals and audio, we have 2 sets of handles: Top ones are for audio and the bottom ones are for visual fades."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Keyframing can be done by pressing the diamond next to them, once a property has a keyframe it will automatically start recording changes which are made on time stamps where no keyframe has been made yet."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Text & Colors"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "We have video, pck, audio, and image files. Those are the files we can drag and drop into the editor. As for text and colors, those are also files but have to be created inside of the editor by pressing the file icon in the top right corner of the file panel."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Rendering your videos"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Probably the most important part besides being able to edit videos is rendering them. There are pre-made render profiles to choose from, but you can of course make your own as well."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Default render profile:"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Want to just render out a region? Use the region shortcuts to easily define which part of your project which you want to export."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Region in:"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Region out:"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Quick note for rendering with custom settings"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Rendering speeds can vary greatly depending on which render settings you choose. We give you access to the render settings to export the video the way you want, but if you aren't certain what these values do, it's best to stick with the default render profiles to avoid long rendering times and/or giant file sizes."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Modularity in GoZen"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Modules can be used for extending the editor. Want extra panels which add functionality to the editor, or maybe you want some nice shiny effects, or there's a specific transition you want for your project? You can do that with modules."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "To add modules you can click \"Preferences\" in the menu bar and click on \"Module manager\"."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Itch.io modules"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Steam workshop"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Custom PCK files"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Modules change the editor and add functionality to the editor, but there's another type of modules refered to as pck files. These are Godot scene's which can be used directly in the timeline for visuals. For the creation of these files a bit of development is needed inside of custom Godot project."
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "PCK Module Project"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid "Workspaces"
msgstr ""

#: scenes/welcome/welcome.tscn
msgid ""
"Workspaces in GoZen are the different tabs which can be accessed in the top right corner. The default ones are \"Edit\" and \"Render\". You can create more and through the \"View\" tab in the menu bar you can choose which panels should be visible in each tab and create new workspaces.\n"
"\n"
"To quickly switch between workspaces you can use CTRL+Enter, this will move you to the next workspace."
msgstr ""

